PA11 resolution — A dependency guard checks direct host identity, registration, count eligibility, HZ inputs, deletion, and the stored tally before inactive-world culling. Unchanged direct-host planets skip locking, vector searches, and HZ calculations. Unusual ancestry retains full synchronization. Verification: all 11 housekeeping tests, 81 active rendering tests, four focused planet tests, and the application build pass; six optional GPU tests remain skipped. Repeated culls retain location and unique membership, while SMA, mass-cutoff, and deletion edits refresh counts.

[x] PA12 — Baseline constellation regression: the ExoConsTest fixture reloads authored lines without resolving their vantage points or endpoints. Validate the fixture against the application loading sequence and restore meaningful authored-shape coverage.
[ ] PA13 — Baseline catalog-photometry regression: 48 star/epoch comparisons exceed the catalog brightness tolerance. Diagnose source values, orbit restoration, variability, and fixture assumptions before changing photometry.

Audit baseline measurements — Horizon pan/travel CPU timings were 145.573/147.226 ms per frame, with geometry digests 7655857646849706811/9311653575339938713. A controlled 100,000-record JSON workload used 178,820 KiB peak RSS with dump(4), versus 120,608 KiB with streaming; elapsed times were 0.75/0.68 seconds. These measurements isolate allocation behavior and are not whole-application FPS claims. Callgrind can collect software instruction traces despite hardware-counter restrictions.

PA01 resolution — save_all now streams four-space formatted JSON directly from the DOM, eliminating the complete dump string. All 68 serialization checks pass, including exact Unicode/escape/nested-object/empty-document bytes in both save modes. The full 17-suite run introduces no additional failures: PA11 passes, while the five disabled-condensation expectations, PA12, and PA13 reproduce their baseline results. All 81 active rendering checks pass; six optional GPU checks remain skipped. The application builds. The controlled save workload lowered peak RSS by 58,212 KiB (32.6%).

[ ] PA14 — Texture loading creates one detached operating-system thread per task, without a concurrency bound (src/loaders.cpp). A burst of visible worlds or regeneration requests can oversubscribe CPU and multiply thread stacks. Replace this with a bounded worker queue while retaining every accepted task, complete map resolution, object-lifetime accounting, cancellation rejection, and shutdown waiting.

Additional review coverage — Texture uploads already track map generations; galaxy image and missing-file caches avoid repeated image decoding; sky-gradient uploads are frame-scoped; shader timer queries poll availability. Startup download freshness and condensed-catalog paths have regression coverage. Shore searches run on demand, satellite-center lookup runs on installation, and stellar chemistry indexes its sources once. Preserve idle throttling, full-resolution surface/cloud sampling, dynamic eclipse ordering, alert semantics, and transactional import behavior. None of these observations justifies reducing scene detail.

